    "intro_html":  "Taiwanese beef noodle is the closest thing Taiwan has to a national dish, and it is a serious bowl, not a thin soup with a few pieces of meat floating in it. Chuck roast braises in soy sauce and doubanjiang until it falls apart, and the broth that comes out of it is worth the afternoon by itself. Each bowl runs 628 calories and \u003cstrong\u003e38 grams of protein\u003c/strong\u003e for about \u003cstrong\u003e$6.21 a serving\u003c/strong\u003e (at everyday cost).",
